--- RAST --->
# **the teardown is one call at the drop site and a branch inside the body.** the `if` exists once per type,
# which is the whole dividend of the pair being a layout rather than a flag: at a use site there is nothing
# conditional, so an argument, a return and a property all work with no rule of their own
CHECK: call $deinit(addrof<Grid?&>(varref<Grid?>(var($present))))
CHECK: function $deinit -> type<void>
CHECK: if (ma<bool>(varref<Grid?&>(var($this))->__has))
CHECK: call $deinit(addrof<Grid&>(ma<Grid>(varref<Grid?&>(var($this))->__value)))
